{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For they became holy</b> — the firepans, and they are forbidden for personal use, for they had already been made into service vessels — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 17:2). But I do not know the reason for this prohibition, for they offered alien incense, and a layperson who makes a service vessel to offer outside is not consecrated. But one may say that because they did so at Moses' instruction, they were holy, for they consecrated them to Heaven because they thought that Elohim would answer them with fire, and these firepans would be service vessels in the Tent of Meeting forever. And what seems correct in my eyes is that Scripture says, \"For they presented them before YHWH and they became holy, and they shall be a sign for the children of Israel\" (Numbers 17:3) — meaning, I consecrated them from the time they presented them before Me, so that they would be a sign for the children of Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:22.554275133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}